sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as WordPress Admin
    participant Workbench as Workbench UI (WorkbenchRoute)
    participant Hook as useRecognitionJob
    participant API as WP REST API
    participant Service as RecognitionService (PHP)
    participant Backend as Recognition API (HF Spaces)
    participant Storage as Media Library

    Note over Admin,Backend: Face Recognition with Roster Management
    Admin->>Workbench: Open media item in Workbench
    Workbench->>Storage: Load attachment metadata & thumbnail
    Admin->>Workbench: Click "Run Recognition" (bulk action)
    Workbench->>Hook: runRecognition(selectedIds)
    Hook->>API: POST /recognition/analyze (attachment IDs)
    API->>Service: analyzeAttachments(ids)
    Service->>Backend: POST /api/v0/analyze-scene (attachment URL)
    Note over Backend: Backend performs:<br/>1. Face detection<br/>2. Embedding extraction<br/>3. Roster matching<br/>4. Confidence scoring
    Backend-->>Service: SceneAnalysisResult (faces, matched roster entries, confidence)
    Service->>Storage: Store observations + roster matches in post_meta
    Service-->>API: RecognitionJobSummary (jobId, status, stats)
    API-->>Hook: Job created successfully
    Hook->>Hook: Poll job status (useRecognitionPoll)
    Hook-->>Workbench: Display recognition results + observations panel
    Note over Admin: Operator can review observations:<br/>- View matched roster entries<br/>- Assign/reassign matches<br/>- Create new roster entries<br/>- Navigate to Roster Manager
    Admin->>Workbench: Navigate to Roster Manager
    Workbench->>API: GET /roster (full CRUD interface)
    API-->>Workbench: Display roster entries
    Note over Admin: Roster Manager supports:<br/>- Create/Edit/Delete entries (useRoster hook)<br/>- Sync with backend roster<br/>- Upload reference images<br/>- Review pending observations (useRecognitionObservations)
